  "qualified_scope": [
    "This exact source executed the bounded captured-C post-test application on actual Linux x86_64 and Linux AArch64 host processes. Host reports, compiled LP64 probes, matching ELF machines and direct command records agree.",
    "The retained protocol is hepta.hia.c-posttest-native-host-protocol.v2: four captured C translation units, eleven unchanged upstream bodies, one authored checksum_byte body changed from for to an eight-iteration post-test loop, and a separately authored integration client.",
    "For each architecture, 48 functional inputs were evaluated through HIA Core-to-target-LLVM-object, original Clang C and independent GNU C: 144 function calls in three batch processes. Sixteen resource cases were evaluated through C and HIA: 32 resource processes.",
    "The resource matrix uses counts 0/1/8/9 and normal execution plus refusal of allocation 1/2/3; the checked native and VM observations agree on attempts, successful allocations, frees, zero remaining live allocations and returned values.",
    "Each architecture separately passed the same twelve native-host control methods. These and the application observations are separate evidence from the earlier local x86_64 43-control gate and 277-method canonical safety matrix."
  ],
  "remaining_boundaries": [
    "physical_hardware_attested remains false. Hosted-runner uname/ABI/ELF agreement does not qualify a named physical board, prove its hardware configuration, or establish bare-metal behavior.",
    "No MMIO, DMA, interrupt, device fault recovery, whole-process RSS bound, WCET or general real-time qualification is established.",
    "This AArch64 execution used the object-file/scalar-C-ABI profile. General shared-image/JIT support, arbitrary foreign-pointer ABI and other operating systems or architectures do not follow.",
    "These finite observations do not prove source equivalence, backend refinement, whole-language soundness, all C/C++ migration, or Rust performance superiority.",
    "The separate CRC run41017483894 remains failed. This successful workflow does not make every CI check or every user acceptance condition pass.",
    "This is the checksum post-test maintenance profile, not the separate 96-combination ring_buffer_queue_arr maintenance experiment; their case counts must not be conflated."
